    "title": "Go Behind the Scenes of This Year’s Best Picture Oscar Nominees",
    "text": "The Oscars Takeaways Best Picture Winners Unforgettable Looks Stream the Winners Top to bottom, scenes from “Marty Supreme,” “Sentimental Value” and “Sinners.” Credit... Top to bottom; A24, Neon, Warner Bros. Skip to content Skip to site index anatomy of a Scene Go Behind the Scenes of This Year’s Best Picture Oscar Nominees In these videos, directors walked us through pivotal sequences from their 2026 Academy Award-nominated films. Top to bottom, scenes from “Marty Supreme,” “Sentimental Value” and “Sinners.” Credit... Top to bottom; A24, Neon, Warner Bros. Supported by SKIP ADVERTISEMENT Listen · 1:38 min Share full article 53 By Mekado Murphy Published March 13, 2026 Updated March 16, 2026 You can learn a great deal about a movie from just one scene. Some act as microcosms for a film’s theme. Others help paint a clear picture of character motivations. And others just want to dazzle. A few of the scenes you’ll find here from the best picture nominees at the 2026 Academy Awards on Sunday were among the most talked about of the year. “Sinners” packs decades of Black music history inside of one sweeping shot. “Train Dreams” uses a plane ride to sum up the totality of a man’s life. Two films unlock emotions on theatrical stages and a third takes a moment to pause in a place where that act can be most detrimental: on a race track. Below, the directors behind eight of the 10 best picture contenders narrate sequences from their work and what motivated them. (Paul Thomas Anderson, who directed “One Battle After Another,” and Yorgos Lanthimos, who directed “Bugonia,” declined to be interviewed.) The filmmakers explain how a lighting choice, a camera move, a well-timed edit or a great piece of dialogue can enliven a sequence and get to the core of a movie’s meaning. Enjoy the show. Joseph Kosinski on ‘F1’ Video ‘F1’ | Anatomy of a Scene 1:17 Joseph Kosinski narrates a sequence from his film, starring Brad Pitt. Credit Credit... Apple Original Films F1: The Movie Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Guillermo del Toro on ‘Frankenstein’ Video ‘Frankenstein’ | Anatomy of a Scene 4:35 Guillermo del Toro narrates a sequence from his film, starring “Oscar Isaac.” Credit Credit... Ken Woroner/Netflix Frankenstein Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Chloé Zhao on ‘Hamnet’ Video ‘Hamnet’ | Anatomy of a Scene 2:22 The director Chloé Zhao narrates a sequence from her Oscar-nominated film, featuring Jessie Buckley and Paul Mescal. Credit Credit... Agata Grzybowska/Focus Features Hamnet Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Josh Safdie on ‘Marty Supreme’ Video ‘Marty Supreme’ | Anatomy of a Scene 3:17 The director Josh Safdie narrates a sequence from his film, nominated for nine Oscars and featuring Timothée Chalamet and Gwyneth Paltrow. Credit Credit... A24 Marty Supreme Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Kleber Mendonça Filho on ‘The Secret Agent’ Video ‘The Secret Agent’ | Anatomy of a Scene 5:34 The director Kleber Mendonça Filho narrates an ensemble sequence from his film, which is nominated for best picture. Credit Credit... Neon The Secret Agent Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Joachim Trier on ‘Sentimental Value’ Video ‘Sentimental Value’ | Anatomy of a Scene 4:56 The director Joachim Trier narrates a sequence from his film. Credit Credit... Kasper Tuxen/Neon, via Associated Press Sentimental Value Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Ryan Coogler on ‘Sinners’ Video ‘Sinners’ | Anatomy of a Scene 2:05 Ryan Coogler narrates a musical sequence from “Sinners,” in which the past and future of Black music is conjured. Credit Credit... Warner Bros. Pictures Sinners Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Clint Bentley on ‘Train Dreams’ Video ‘Train Dreams’ | Anatomy of a Scene 2:33 The director Clint Bentley narrates a sequence from his film starring Joel Edgerton. Credit Credit... Netflix Train Dreams Save to your watch list : Want to watch Have seen Mekado Murphy writes about the world of movies and produces the Anatomy of a Scene video series. See more on: Academy Awards (Oscars) , Guillermo Del Toro , Yorgos Lanthimos , Josh Safdie Read 53 comments Share full article 53 Related Content Advertisement SKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
